window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-1b4988583b9cbd21"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"_1\">清理并审阅财务模型</h1> <p>在重要审阅前检查公式、链接、勾稽关系和假设。</p> <p>提供财务模型及其支持来源，让 ChatGPT 安全地清理文件，并生成按严重程度排序的 QA 备忘录，说明公式风险、失效链接、来源勾稽问题，以及需要负责人审阅的假设。</p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要在领导层、投资者或董事会审阅前核验公式和来源的财务模型。</li> <li>包含硬编码数值、失效链接、期间不一致或检查项含义不清的工作簿。</li> <li>需要将安全清理与业务假设变更分开处理的团队。</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>检查工作簿结构和公式，进行安全编辑，并渲染清理后的模型供审阅。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>清理并审阅模型</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 $spreadsheets，在将 [model name] 提交给 [audience] 之前，对其进行清理和审阅。\n\n检查工作簿结构、公式、硬编码数值、失效链接、循环引用、正负号约定、期间标签、来源勾稽、模型检查项和输出工作表。请重点检查 [priority tabs or outputs]。\n\n只有在预期逻辑明确时，才进行安全清理和公式修正。未经批准，不要更改业务假设。请返回可编辑的清理后工作簿，以及按严重程度排序的 QA 备忘录，列出发现的问题、已做的修复、仍未解决的假设，以及需要财务负责人审阅的具体单元格或工作表。将原始文件保留为单独的输入文件。\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">智能体技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">引言</h2> <p>财务模型中经常会逐渐积累隐藏的硬编码数值、过时链接、期间不一致，以及无法与来源勾稽的检查项。ChatGPT 可以系统地检查工作簿，只做范围明确的修正，并生成 QA 备忘录，指出哪些地方仍需财务负责人作判断。</p> <h2 id=\"_6\">明确审阅边界</h2> <p>附上模型及其应当勾稽的来源文件。说明审阅对象、优先工作表、预期输出，以及哪些假设不得更改。保留原始工作簿，以便逐项对比修改内容。</p> <ol> <li>附上模型及其支持来源文件。</li> <li>指明优先工作表、预期检查项和受保护的假设。</li> <li>运行起始提示词，要求返回清理后的副本和 QA 备忘录。</li> <li>在 ChatGPT 中打开工作簿，检查变更过的公式、链接和输出工作表。</li> <li>接受假设变更前，先解决财务负责人的疑问。</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"_7\">检查清理结果</h2> <p>QA 备忘录应按严重程度排列问题，并指向具体单元格或工作表。可以直接修复安全的格式、标签问题和明确的公式错误；对于含义不清的业务逻辑，应保留问题标记，等待审阅。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare the cleaned model with the original.\n\nList:\n\n- formulas, links, or checks that changed\n- source tie-outs that now pass or still fail\n- hardcodes and assumptions that remain\n- circular references or sign issues\n- output tabs affected by the changes\n- items that require finance-owner approval\n\nDo not make additional assumption changes. Return a concise change log with exact cell or tab references.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">将清理后的模型与原始模型进行比较。\n\n列出：\n\n- 发生变化的公式、链接或检查\n- 现在已通过或仍未通过的来源数据勾稽核对\n- 仍然存在的硬编码值和假设\n- 循环引用或正负号问题\n- 受到这些更改影响的输出工作表\n- 需要财务负责人批准的事项\n\n不要额外更改任何假设。返回简明的变更记录，并给出准确的单元格或工作表引用。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"clean-and-review-a-financial-model\">Clean and review a financial model</h1> <p>Check formulas, links, tie-outs, and assumptions before a high-stakes review.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT a financial model and its supporting sources, then ask it to make safe cleanup changes and return a severity-ranked QA memo covering formula risks, broken links, source tie-outs, and assumptions that need an owner.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Financial models that need formula and source QA before leadership, investor, or board review.</li> <li>Workbooks with hardcodes, broken links, inconsistent periods, or unclear checks.</li> <li>Teams that want safe cleanup separated from business-assumption changes.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Inspect workbook structure and formulas, make safe edits, and render the cleaned model for review.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Clean and review the model</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $spreadsheets to clean and review [model name] before it goes to [audience].\n\nInspect workbook structure, formulas, hardcodes, broken links, circular references, sign conventions, period labels, source tie-outs, model checks, and output tabs. Pay special attention to [priority tabs or outputs].\n\nMake safe cleanup and formula fixes where the intended behavior is clear. Do not change business assumptions without approval. Return an editable cleaned workbook plus a severity-ranked QA memo with issues found, fixes made, remaining assumptions, and the exact cells or tabs that need finance-owner review. Preserve the original file as a separate input.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>Financial models often accumulate hidden hardcodes, stale links, inconsistent periods, and checks that no longer tie. ChatGPT can inspect the workbook systematically, make narrowly scoped fixes, and produce a QA memo that tells a finance owner where judgment is still required.</p> <h2 id=\"define-the-review-boundary\">Define the review boundary</h2> <p>Attach the model and the source files it should tie to. Name the audience, priority tabs, expected outputs, and any assumptions ChatGPT must leave unchanged. Keep the original workbook available so you can compare every edit.</p> <ol> <li>Attach the model and its supporting source files.</li> <li>Identify priority tabs, expected checks, and protected assumptions.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and request a cleaned copy plus a QA memo.</li> <li>Open the workbook in ChatGPT and inspect changed formulas, links, and output tabs.</li> <li>Resolve finance-owner questions before accepting assumption changes.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"check-the-cleanup\">Check the cleanup</h2> <p>The QA memo should rank issues by severity and point to exact cells or tabs. Safe formatting, labeling, and clear formula repairs can be applied directly; ambiguous business logic should remain flagged for review.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Compare the cleaned model with the original.\n\nList:\n\n- formulas, links, or checks that changed\n- source tie-outs that now pass or still fail\n- hardcodes and assumptions that remain\n- circular references or sign issues\n- output tabs affected by the changes\n- items that require finance-owner approval\n\nDo not make additional assumption changes. Return a concise change log with exact cell or tab references.\n</code></pre>"};
